id: pm-gh1556
title: "GH-1556: diagnose ignored merge-receipt paths before settlement staging"
description: "The October23 report identifies raw git add failure when legacy ignore rules hide merge-receipts that current settlement must commit. Reproduce with a real temporary Git repository, diagnose the owning ignore rule before staging, and keep settlement/history preservation and typed SDK/CLI recovery intact."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1556",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T07:34:10.262Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T20:34:46.530Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e495e5b5774b85b06e5f8657"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: A real Git fixture reproduces ignored receipt staging without source tracker access; Refusal names the ignore rule and safe remedy before ambiguous partial staging; Health/upgrade guidance reflects committed receipt requirements and normal settlement remains idempotent.
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: Legacy ignored merge receipts produce typed actionable recovery naming the ignore rule and preserving unsettled proof; ordinary settlement and exact history verification continue to pass.
