comments[6]:
  - created_at: "2026-10-23T07:34:10.262Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Intake: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1556. Duplicate checks used request-specific live search and a fresh all-status strict corpus of3071 items with no omissions; related delivered lineage is linked and remains closed. The report is recorded without claiming current reproduction. Intake only, open and unclaimed."
  - created_at: "2026-10-24T20:03:49.211Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Active implementation: reproduce ignored merge-receipt staging in a real isolated Git fixture, refuse with owning ignore-rule diagnostics before any staging or audit writes, and expose proactive health/upgrade guidance. Grouped SDK merge delivery with pm-gh1553. GitHub currently reports no open PRs or security alerts; every open issue has canonical PM linkage."
  - created_at: "2026-10-24T20:07:06.926Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Added a real Git regression around existing portable-proof acceptance: an ignored receipt must refuse both dry-run and apply with merge_settlement_review_required, exact .gitignore rule coordinates, unchanged index/history/receipt bytes, and a proactive health warning. The current implementation is being exercised as the negative control before the fix."
  - created_at: "2026-10-24T20:19:00.017Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Local acceptance now covers typed ignored-path recovery in dry-run and apply, proactive health detection from .gitignore and .git/info/exclude before any receipt exists, exact NUL decoding/negation semantics, unavailable Git evidence refusal and new-index-entry rollback even when Git fails during preparation. Existing normal/alternate index and LF/CRLF preservation cases remain intact. Health composition is factored through its existing merge-evidence helper to preserve the complexity limit."
  - created_at: "2026-10-24T20:28:46.595Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Health evidence correction: the long read-only health scan reported history_drift_hash_mismatch for pm-gh1553 while tracker updates were in flight. A fresh pm history pm-gh1553 --verify proves15 valid entries, zero errors, and current_matches_latest=true; no repair was applied. Full history-drift validation passes, with170 historical resolution metadata advisories. A quiet follow-up health scan will distinguish the transient observation from current drift. Latest npm pm-changelog2026.10.24 installs/activates; package doctor has zero load/activation/blocking failures and advisory partial update-check coverage."
    edited_at: "2026-10-24T20:29:44.941Z"
  - created_at: "2026-10-24T20:34:46.527Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Quiet verification completed: pm health --check-only --full --skip-vectors returns ok=true with zero blocking findings and only14 existing legacy hierarchy advisories. The earlier transient mismatch is absent, and no history repair was applied. Candidate packed smoke timed out before packaging while waiting on the full-coverage build lease; it will be rerun sequentially after coverage/static completion. No packed-consumer success is inferred from that timeout."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-24T20:23:10.569Z","harness:codex","Portable merge receipts depend on effective Git policy from project, nested, clone-local and global ignore sources. Check effective rules with Git's NUL stdin/output protocol before staging or audit writes; preserve native negations and tracked-file semantics, and rollback newly prepared index entries on partial preparation failure."
